-- Boundary module: Public Service Act 1999 (Cth) s 39, Heads of Mission, which the
-- Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 meets at ss 9(1) and 14(1)-(3).
-- Source: Public Service Act 1999, Compilation No. 22, compilation date 11 December 2024,
-- register ID C2024C00795 (source bundle item cth-psa-1999).
-- Reference register: REF-16 (s 39 and s 7 'Head of Mission').
--
-- Two byte-identical copies of this file exist: psa-1999-s39.l4 in the subject folder, which the Bill's
-- modules import, and boundary/psa-1999-s39.l4, the path the reference register names. The installed l4
-- cannot import from another folder (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-01).

§ `Public Service Act 1999 s 7 -- Head of Mission`

-- s 7: "Head of Mission means the head of: (a) an Australian diplomatic mission; or (b) an
-- Australian consular mission." Whether an office is the head of such a mission is a fact the
-- caller supplies (the Bill's offices in s 7(1) all are; an office prescribed under s 7(2) may
-- not be).

§ `Public Service Act 1999 s 39 -- Heads of Mission`

-- s 39(1): "The appointment of a Head of Mission by the Governor-General cannot take effect
-- unless the person is an APS employee."
@ref Public Service Act 1999 s 39(1)
GIVEN `made by the Governor-General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office is that of a Head of Mission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an APS employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 39(1) lets the appointment take effect` `made by the Governor-General` `the office is that of a Head of Mission` `the person is an APS employee` IF
        (NOT (`made by the Governor-General` AND `the office is that of a Head of Mission`))
     OR `the person is an APS employee`

-- s 39(2): "An Agency Head must comply with any direction in writing by the Agency Minister:
-- (a) directing the Agency Head to engage a particular person as an APS employee so that the
-- person can become a Head of Mission; or (b) directing the Agency Head to assign particular
-- duties to an APS employee who has been appointed as a Head of Mission."
-- Encoded as the route by which a person who is not an APS employee can become one: if the
-- Agency Minister so directs and the Agency Head complies, the person is an APS employee.
@ref Public Service Act 1999 s 39(2)(a)
GIVEN `already an APS employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `engaged under a direction under s 39(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an APS employee after any s 39(2)(a) engagement` `already an APS employee` `engaged under a direction under s 39(2)(a)` IF
        `already an APS employee`
     OR `engaged under a direction under s 39(2)(a)`
